WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.940
A seaside "Good job!"

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.400
Hurry up!

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.000
You're my dearest.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.910
I've kept it pent up in my heart

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.470
because you were too close.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.410
The waves sound good!

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.410
They are the 77th generation.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.970
My heart jumps for joy.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.540
Orine! You're falling behind!

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:29.340
This year, I'll be more earnest than ever.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:21.700
Right!

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.870
The training is tough,
but as long as their friends are by their side,
they can make it together.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.470
Day by day,
they learn and grow...
until the day they bloom like a flower.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.470
manatsu no Sounds good!

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.470
A midsummer "Sounds good!"

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.180
Whose name would you like to inherit?

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:36.280
kimi ga suki da

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:36.280
I love you so.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.760
I-It'd be an honor to succeed anyone! Yes!

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.310
nagisa no Good job!

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.310
A seaside "Good job!"

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:42.810
I love you so.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.430
Sonata wants to be Love-tan!

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:46.150
I would like to succeed Sashiko-san.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:45.470
kikkake Good job!

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:45.470
Here's my chance, "Good job!"

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:49.150
Talk about good timing.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.150
Their eyes are fixed
on their brilliant futures.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.900
manatsu no Sounds good!

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.900
A midsummer "Sounds good!"

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:58.620
Support the 77th generation on their road ahead!

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.810
That was your promotional video that we filmed a few days ago.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.630
Oh my God! Just look at my waist!

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:07.760
It's unsightly!

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:09.490
Orine, you looked cute!

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.670
Two centimeters! All I wanted was two centimeters off my waist!

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.070
There's no use worrying now.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:17.070
The video has been broadcast not only on Akibastar, but throughout the galaxy.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:18.370
You're kidding.

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:22.490
Now the galaxy will know me as the whale-waisted idol.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:23.810
Listen up.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:28.040
The 77th generation's public debut is coming up soon.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:32.520
It's a handshake event, not a concert, on a planet in the Entertainment Protection Sphere.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.370
We're debuting at a handshake event?

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:35.320
Indeed.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:40.830
Handshake events are very important for members of AKB0048.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:46.800
It's your best opportunity to meet your fans and get their feedback in person.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:47.960
Right you are!

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.180
Takamina-san!

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:50.170
Yukirin-san.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:51.400
Sayaka!

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.020
Good morning!

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:53.920
Morning!

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:57.000
As you know, we're the idols who come to see you.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.620
We're also the idols you can touch.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:04.430
Your behavior at the event will have a huge impact on your popularity.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:05.390
Really?

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.140
If you want to make the most of this opportunity,

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:10.950
you first need a firm handshake!

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.900
Ow ow ow!

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.610
Then, you need to make eye contact and smile!

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:20.780
It's also vital to acknowledge each and every fan.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.620
Acknowledge?

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:26.450
Be sure to remember their names, faces, and what they said.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:26.620
Kyotostar

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:26.790
Thank you~!!

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:31.310
Wow.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:32.880
Don't forget your outfit!

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.180
Since it's only a handshake event,

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:38.090
you're free to choose the outfit that brings out the best in you.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:43.090
You can please or disappoint your fans depending on your choice.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.590
I never knew clothes were such a big deal!

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:47.870
What do I do?

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.600
The only proper outfit I have is my school uniform!

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.290
Wanna borrow some of mine?

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.000
I'd be happy to lend some, too.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.270
Really?

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.690
Bad idea.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:00.250
Takamina and Yukirin are the Twin Towers of bad fashion.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.160
What?!

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.800
But it's true!

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.130
Our outfit, huh?

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:07.510
Well, we don't have lessons until the afternoon.

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:08.960
Yeah.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.950
Ready, set, here we go!

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.000
AKB0048!

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:32.050
Even if you reach out your hand,

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:32.070
sono te nobashitemo

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:38.640
you won't be able to reach it yet.

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:38.640
ima wa ima wa todokanai yo

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:44.230
Our dreams still lie

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:44.230
bokutachi no yume wa

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:49.820
much, much further in the distance.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.700
Even the stars of the sky

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.950
lie billions of lightyears away,

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:02.830
shining beyond the shadows.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:09.090
Let me speak of hope,

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:15.180
like a nameless poet: with passion.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.390
you ni

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.180
atsuku

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:21.230
If you find yourself broken down in tears,

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:21.230
kimi ga namida ni kureteiru nara

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:26.690
then rather than consoling you,

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:33.360
let me speak of the coming dawn.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:43.210
- Handshake Debut-

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.300
Are you done yet?

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.930
Hang on a second!

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.710
Ta-dah!

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:50.600
Ta-dah!

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.560
Ta-da-dah!

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.190
Augh, I don't even know anymore!

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:00.320
My mind is spinny spinny spinning away...

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.440
This thing costs 30,000!

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.110
I only have 2,000 on me.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:05.020
So it wasn't an option in the first place.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.660
We ended up not buying anything.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.440
Nagisa, just don't wear your school uniform.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:14.950
Huh? Why?

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:17.750
We've got mail!

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:19.760
Looky, looky!

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.860
A fan letter for Orine!

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:22.860
What?

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:24.220
Oh my goodness!

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.830
That's great, Orine!

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:30.180
But I... I haven't even debuted...

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.880
I'll bet they saw the promotional video.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.290
Someone's already investing in your potential, Orine!

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.610
They sent a file instead of a letter.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.860
I'll get my cell phone and we'll play it.

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:42.280
Okay.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:50.450
Aida Orine-san.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.410
You've got some funny ideas in your head, bitch.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:59.290
To become Sashiko, you need the power

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:58.210
This is...

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:03.280
to maximize your uselessness and turn that negative energy into positive energy.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:05.690
You're so wishy-washy, it's disgusting.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.420
Your dancing sucks. It's lifeless.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:08.880
You don't have what it takes to be a star.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:13.360
You'll regret spouting that arrogant nonsense about becoming Sashiko.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:18.350
Your presence in AKB0048, Aida Orine,

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:16.810
Oh gosh! That's enough.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.350
Hey, I can't close it!

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:23.320
is a stain upon the 00 I love.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:26.990
You'd better quit 00 before that handshake event.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:30.400
Otherwise, I'll set off a bomb at the event location, and put an end—

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.340
What do you think you're doing?

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:33.860
Tsubasa-san.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:37.290
You can't read fan mail until we've screened it.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:42.290
I wasn't expecting it so soon, so our screening was lax.

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:45.630
Orine...

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.830
There's nothing to get worked up about.

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:49.630
We get these sorts of letters all the time.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.390
But...

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:55.600
The last Sashiko graduated only two years ago.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.390
She was very popular.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:02.490
The more popular and noticeable a
member is, the more haters they attract.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:05.360
The same goes for those who aspire to that name.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.360
Haters...?

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:12.690
If you lose your spirit over this, you don't stand a chance in the future.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:14.700
But he made a bomb threat!

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:18.580
AKB0048 members must face DES forces in combat.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:21.590
We can't afford to back down from every threat.

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:23.980
Stand your ground, girls.

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:27.860
You'll let down tons of fans over one little hater.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:29.340
That is unacceptable.

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:32.700
Come, it's time.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.440
Head to the practice room.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:35.810
Okay...

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.730
<i>You're so wishy-washy, it's disgusting.</i>

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:00.120
Okay! Okay! Okay! Okay!

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:03.610
Put your backs into it!

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:04.130
Right!

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.090
<i>"Your dancing sucks. It's lifeless."</i>

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:10.010
<i>"You don't have what it takes to be a star."</i>

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.700
Where is your mind wandering off to, Orine?

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.470
I'm sorry!

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:23.120
Get a grip on yourself.

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:27.170
You seriously let that get to you?

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:30.500
Do you expect to become a successor like that?

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:35.450
Chieri, you didn't have to put it that way!

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.370
Orine!

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:38.660
Now hold on...

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:40.490
Wait, Orine!

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:43.120
Why did you have to say that?

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:45.420
You saw the video, too!

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:49.860
Nobody could keep their cool after seeing that.

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:50.880
That's the issue.

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:55.770
I don't want her to give up because of this.

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:57.340
Otherwise...

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:01.420
my dream won't come true.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:06.700
<i>Our... dream...</i>

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:08.740
Are you talking about—

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:11.460
Oh, for the love of...

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:16.730
I'll go bring them back. You five, continue practicing.

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:17.410
Okay.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:23.630
Chieri...

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.770
Can't hold it any longer!

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:32.150
Hey, what's wrong?

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:33.380
Are you okay?

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:38.300
Ah, Orine.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.270
Huh?

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.030
What's wrong?

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:49.940
Here.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:51.640
I'm sorry.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:55.070
Everyone has their haters.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.030
Even you?

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.330
Yep.

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:03.390
Successors of Takamina are
designated as the team captains.

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:06.500
"Unreliable." "Lacks aura."
You wouldn't believe it.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:10.300
There are still people like that, even now.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:12.960
Why would they say such awful things?

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:15.830
You think it's awful?

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:22.810
I forgot! Nature calls!

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:26.500
I <i>really</i> can't hold it anymore!

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:47.500
You know how my parents are gone, right?

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:53.360
Luckily, I had wonderful friends like you and Yuuka,

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:56.740
and the ladies at the factory were so nice to me.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:59.630
Even so, I still couldn't shake the thought...

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:03.890
that nobody was really watching me.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.760
That's not true.

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:08.610
I wanted people to see me.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:10.260
But...

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:15.360
I guess being seen by people is scarier than I thought.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.710
It's okay.

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:21.820
I'll still show up at the handshake event.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:25.780
Takamina-san told me that everyone has their haters.

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:30.270
That's just part of being in 00.

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:34.760
Orine...

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:44.050
Originally, there were "special" and "national" handshake events.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:39.800
Handshake Event

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:48.770
However, 0048's events combine both types.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:50.730
Look at all the people!

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:52.390
They're lining up!

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:53.440
We're starting now.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:57.360
Your handshaking begins at 1:50 PM.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:00.740
When the other members go on break this afternoon, you'll take their place.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:04.160
You'll be split into two lanes: a group of four and a group of three.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.950
I can't wait!

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:11.120
Once you're changed, just wait for your entrance.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:11.910
Understand?

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.080
Yes!

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:17.170
Sonata, you're wearing <i>that?</i>

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:18.800
I've got bunny ears today!

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:24.680
So you <i>did</i> choose your school uniform!

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:27.550
Well, they still count as nice clothes.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:30.390
At least you're not the worst of them.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:31.680
You call that an outfit?

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:32.230
Are you serious?

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:35.650
There's never been a moment when I <i>wasn't</i> serious.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:37.310
What?

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.150
The heiress of Zodiac Corporation, missing or kidnapped...?

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:41.440
<i>Is she just trying to avoid being taken home?</i>

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:42.900
Sheesh.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:45.570
I'll lend you one of mine, so put it on.

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:46.160
Take it.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:53.540
You don't have to if you don't want to.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.830
I think the boyish look works fine!

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:57.380
What?

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:58.540
Thank you.

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:03.130
I'm so sorry.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.010
Orine.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:05.720
Are you okay?

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:09.260
Orine...

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:13.730
Okay, it's almost time.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:15.890
Orine, can you manage?

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.610
Yes.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:21.360
Don't worry, we've got your back!

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.490
So does Sonata!

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:24.950
And Grumbly's gonna help, too.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:28.450
Grumbly's gonna make a great shield for Sonata and Orine!

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:29.620
I am <i>not</i> a shield!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:33.370
Thank you, everyone.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.100
Not a lot of people, huh?

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:56.060
We should have expected this, but it still stinks.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.850
Excuse me, Aida Orine-san?

00:13:58.850 --> 00:13:59.480
Yes?

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:06.360
This girl just went on and on about how cute you were after seeing your video.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.030
She's an Orine fan?

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:11.910
That's wonderful!

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:15.500
Go on, Yayoi. Ask her to shake your hand.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:19.250
P-Please shake my hand!

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:21.710
Orine.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:23.050
You can do it!

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:24.130
Okay.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:31.970
<i>My very first handshake.</i>

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:35.390
Go on, say thank you to the nice girl.

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:36.560
Thank you!

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:37.310
Huh?

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.230
Thank you.

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:41.400
Thank you so much!

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:42.820
Thank goodness!

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:45.480
What are you crying about?

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:48.360
But... But...

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.990
Bye-bye!

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:02.130
See you!

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:09.090
You!

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:12.050
I <i>told</i> you to quit!

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:15.760
Chieri!

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:19.440
What's <i>your</i> problem?!

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:21.730
Nice to meet you!

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:25.360
I'm a 77th generation understudy, Sono Chieri!

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.610
Thank you so much for coming today!

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.200
Don't tell me you seriously...

